---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { LEGAL, LINKS } from '../lib/brand';
---

<LegalLayout title="Licences and credits" description="Licences for Baken, the third-party software it uses, and credits for the artwork on this site.">
  <h2>Baken</h2>
  <p>
    The Baken source is public in the <a href={LINKS.appRepo}>letta-mobile repository</a>.
    {LEGAL.license
      ? <>It is licensed under {LEGAL.license}.</>
      : <>A licence has not been published yet, so the source is currently "source available": you can read, build and run it for your own use, and all other rights are reserved. This page will be updated when a licence is added.</>}
    The source for this website is in the <a href={LINKS.webRepo}>baken-web repository</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party software</h2>
  <p>Key components the apps and this site rely on:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Used for</th><th>Licence</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>letta-code</td><td>Agent runtime on the host</td><td>Apache-2.0</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Iroh</td><td>Encrypted peer-to-peer connection</td><td>MIT / Apache-2.0</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Kotlin, Compose Multiplatform</td><td>App framework</td><td>Apache-2.0</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Rive runtime</td><td>Mascot and mark animation</td><td>MIT</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Astro</td><td>This website</td><td>MIT</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Plus Jakarta Sans</td><td>Typeface</td><td>SIL Open Font License 1.1</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The apps include many further open source libraries. The Android app includes the full list with licence texts in its
    open source licences screen.
  </p>

  <h2>Artwork</h2>
  <p>
    The chart on the homepage is <em>Paskaart van het Vlie en de Marsdiep</em> (1583), from Lucas Jansz. Waghenaer's
    <em>Spieghel der Zeevaerdt</em>, engraved by Joannes van Doetechum (I). It is in the public domain and comes from the
    collection of the Rijksmuseum, Amsterdam (object NG-43), via its open data service. We have converted it to a dithered
    image for this site.
  </p>
  <p>The engravings on the capability cards are also public domain and come from the Rijksmuseum, Amsterdam:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Sea chart of the waters west of Ireland, anonymous, Netherlands, 1658 (NG-501-31).</li>
    <li><em>Hengelaars in boten bij een molen en een baken</em>, Jan van de Velde (II), 1627 (RP-P-1898-A-20535).</li>
    <li><em>Kompas</em>, Isaac Weissenbruch, 1836 (RP-P-OB-30.364).</li>
    <li><em>Gezicht op duinen met vuurtoren en strand</em>, after Coenraet Decker, c. 1685 (RP-P-OB-50.061).</li>
    <li><em>Haven met een vuurtoren</em>, Reinier Zeeman, 1656 (RP-P-OB-12.966).</li>
    <li><em>Verklaring van de werking van een nieuwe Franse semafoor</em> (<em>De Bewonderenswaardige Telegraaph</em>), anonymous, Northern Netherlands, 1794 (RP-P-OB-86.302).</li>
    <li><em>Rivierlandschap met baken</em>, Hermanus Jan Hendrik Rijkelijkhuizen, 1857 (RP-P-OB-73.914).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Section backgrounds, also public domain from the Rijksmuseum:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><em>Strand met vissers</em>, Carel Frederik Curtenius Bentinck, 1824.</li>
    <li><em>Schip in nood bij storm op zee</em>, Johannes Hilverdink, 1861.</li>
    <li><em>Gezicht op een vuurbaken</em> (<em>Houte bake</em>), Joost van Geel, published by Jacob Quack, after 1666 (RP-P-1882-A-6055).</li>
    <li><em>Windroos, met tweeëndertig windrichtingen in zes talen</em> (<em>Tabula anemographica</em>), printed by Johannes Janssonius, 1652–1680 (RP-P-AO-29-18).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Page headers on the download and docs pages, also public domain from the Rijksmuseum:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><em>Kaart van de noordkust van Engeland bij Newcastle upon Tyne</em>, Lucas Jansz. Waghenaer, engraved by Joannes van Doetechum (I), from the <em>Spieghel der Zeevaerdt</em>, 1580–1583 (RP-P-OB-50.147).</li>
    <li><em>Boussole des Vents</em> (wind rose), published by Pieter Mortier (I), Amsterdam, 1702–1703 (RP-P-OB-83.034-278).</li>
  </ul>
</LegalLayout>
